{"title":"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Nine congruent spheres are packed inside a unit cube in such a way that one of them has its center at the center of the cube and each of the others is tangent to the center sphere and to three faces of the cube. What is the radius of each sphere?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/05024453111fde28df23291e7a6d7097b7207ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 1-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\quad \\text{(B) } \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}-3}{2}\\quad \\text{(C) } \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\quad \\text{(D) } \\frac{1}{4}\\quad \\text{(E) } \\frac{\\sqrt{3}(2-\\sqrt2)}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"484\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the cube, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of one of the eight outer spheres, noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7369613b6ec73b8b5653893aea5e2de1d30153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC=2r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Back, in the corner of the unit cube, a smaller cube whose inner corner coincides with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The cube is of dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c47c1dbfeca0fab07bb3183abe9c3de4d0adf464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\times 1\\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" /> and its space diagonal is of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99f089046b752269e77100c333b11d8d72e5895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />. Thus the space diagonal of the unit cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc40b6a7f6d2fe5cec1f6e21d3f2300397af7bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(r\\sqrt3+2r)=\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c3218ca790f4eac4048f34f68433655b19e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/543f1a29214ff2fcfcd22b6ddf7593549cda1c83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(0,1)--(1,1)--(1,0)--cycle); for(int i=0;i&lt;4;++i)draw(rotate(i*90,(.5,.5))*circle((0.25,0.25),0.225)); //draw(circle((0.75,0.25),0.225)); draw(circle((0.5,0.5),0.19),dashed); draw((0,0)--(.5,.5),dotted); dot((.25,.25));dot((.5,.5)); label(&quot;P&quot;,(.25,.25),S);label(&quot;C&quot;,(.5,.5),N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME\" title=\"1990 AHSME\">1990 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1990 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1990\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Prob